Author: Danny Milosavljevic <dannym@friendly-machines.com>
Date: 2026-05-07
Subject: Make TRefItem.GetCopy an explicit override
License: expat

TRefItem.GetCopy has the same signature as the inherited virtual
TLinkedListItem.GetCopy.  In Pascal, "reintroduce" intentionally starts a
*new* virtual method slot instead of overriding the inherited one.  C++
cannot express same-signature non-overriding virtual methods: the derived
method would override implicitly.

The source-level dispatch sites that could observe the difference are the
generic linked-list copy helpers in compiler/cclasses.pas:

  TLinkedList.insertListcopy, line 2136: NewNode2:=NewNode.Getcopy;
  TLinkedList.concatListcopy, line 2151: NewNode2:=NewNode.Getcopy;

For the FPC 2.6.0 compiler sources used by tp2cc, TRefItem is constructed
directly in compiler/symtype.pas and read back by TRefItem casts in
compiler/browcol.pas.  There are no TRefItem descendants, no TRefItem class
reference type, and no uses of insertListcopy or concatListcopy on a
TRefLinkedList.  Therefore changing this declaration to an explicit override
does not change an observed bootstrap call path, and makes the Pascal source
match the C++ dispatch semantics that tp2cc can emit.

--- a/compiler/crefs.pas
+++ b/compiler/crefs.pas
@@ -34,7 +34,7 @@ uses
    TrefItem = class (TLinkedListItem)
      refinfo  : tfileposinfo;
      constructor create(const ARefInfo : tfileposinfo);
-     Function GetCopy:TLinkedListItem;virtual;reintroduce;
+     Function GetCopy:TLinkedListItem;override;
    end;
 
    TRefLinkedList = class(TLinkedList)
